    kind: work_item  # c3cb
    title: "explain lacks --limit/--language/--file/--first; emits 15713 lines for 'main'"  # c3cb
    status: todo_hard  # c3cb
    priority: 2  # c3cb
    parent: INV-rarol-gogag-lapat-hirun-dolif-kavop-vutaj-larij  # c3cb
    tags:  # c3cb
    - dogfood_tranch_03  # c3cb
    - dogfood  # c3cb
    isbefore: []  # c3cb
    duplicate_of: []  # c3cb
    not_duplicate_of: []  # c3cb
    pr_ref:  # c3cb
    description: "**Mechanic**: `explain` accepts only `--path`, `--input`, `-x`, `--with-source`, `--no-source`, `-t TOKENS`, `--provenance`. There is no flag to limit, filter by language, restrict to a single file, or pick the first match. When the same symbol name occurs N times (10 functions named `main` on a typical multi-script repo), the command emits N full sections, despite a help-doc that describes \"Symbol\" (singular).\n\n**Expectation**: The command provides at least one of: language filter, file filter, \"first match\" mode, or per-section limit — bringing its flag set into parity with the sibling `symbols` command.\n\n**Scope**: `explain <name>` for any name that resolves to multiple symbols; common in Python monorepos, Node projects with multiple package.json files, and multi-binary Go projects. On the self-corpus, `explain \"main\"` produces 15,713 stdout lines.\n\n**Exposure**: Any LLM agent budgeting ~10K tokens for \"what does X do?\" who passes an ambiguous name; any developer running interactive exploration on a multi-binary repo.\n\n**Consequence**: Token budgets blow mid-output; the agent loses any chance of seeing the callees of the symbol it actually wanted; the single-section-per-symbol mental model implied by the docs is wrong on every multi-binary codebase.\n\n**Source**: F43.A2 (INDEPENDENT, HIGH).\n\nFiled via tranch 03 dogfood (passes 41-60, substrate sha256 a32c4a31..., HEAD 9a18959071). Tranch state: `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/dogfood_tranch_03/tranch_state.json`."  # c3cb
    fields: {}  # c3cb
